FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com

# OneThing API
OneThing turns a photo, a link or a picked product into a live one-product shop that takes
PayPal payments, or a recommendation page that earns referral commissions through Channel3.

**How a shop is made**
1. `createShop`: start from a photo, a link, or a Channel3 product. Gemini guesses what it
   is, how it's delivered, the price, a short link and the page design. You get back the
   shop's link name and an **admin token**.
2. `updateShop`: correct anything the AI guessed, then set `status: live`.
3. Buyers pay on `https://<host>/<slug>` with PayPal. Sellers read orders and ship them.

**Auth.** Seller endpoints take the shop's admin token in the `x-admin-token` header, or a
**platform API key** (`Authorization: Bearer ot_sk_…`) for marketplaces that make shops for
their own sellers. Buyer endpoints (checkout, access-code verification, downloads) are public.

**Access codes.** A digital product can unlock an app or game instead of shipping a file.
Each paid order gets a code such as `K7QF-M2XP-9HTD`; your app calls `verifyAccessCode`
before unlocking. Raptor Rush on miriogames.com is a live example.

**Agent-ready.** Every live shop is also published for AI shopping agents: an MCP server at
`/api/mcp` with `search_shops`, `get_product`, `create_order` and `get_order`, and the same
four as plain GETs for assistants that can only fetch URLs (`listAgentShops`,
`getAgentProduct`, `orderByLink`, `getAgentOrder`), with `/llms.txt` as the starting point.
Order and status links also have short forms, `/<slug>/buy` and `/o/<order_id>/status`.
An agent can find and order, but the buyer still approves every payment at PayPal.

**Limits.** Calls that cost something are capped per network: 120 checkouts per 10 minutes,
10 new shops an hour and 60 AI requests an hour. Over the cap the reply is a 429 with
`Retry-After`.

All money moves through PayPal (sandbox in this deployment). OneThing never holds card data.


## Authentication
This API uses Custom Header for its authentication.

The parameters that are needed to be sent for this type of authentication are as follows:
+ `x-admin-token` - The shop's admin token, returned once by `createShop`. Keep it secret.

# Group Accounts

Sign in as a seller with an email or a phone number. Shops made while signed in belong to the account.

## Api Account Signin [/api/account/signin]

### signIn [POST]
Signs in with an email address or a phone number, creating the account the first time. There's no password and no verification (sandbox). The response sets the `ot_session` cookie; shops created with it belong to the account and are listed on `/account`. Signing in with an email also claims older shops whose seller email matches. In a browser, sellers can instead use Log in with PayPal (`/api/account/paypal`), which also records the PayPal account their sales are paid into.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Account Signin Request)


    + Body

            {
                "identifier": "maker@example.com"
            }


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Signed in. The `ot_session` cookie is set.

    + Attributes (Api Account Signin Response)


    + Body

            {"id":"Vq3nN8cT0bLx2YwE","email":"maker@example.com","phone":null}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}



## Api Account Signout [/api/account/signout]

### signOut [POST]
Ends this browser's session and clears the `ot_session` cookie.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Done.

    + Attributes (Ok)


    + Body

            {"ok":true}



## Api Account Paypal [/api/account/paypal{?next}]

### logInWithPayPal [GET]
A link for a browser, not for code: redirects to PayPal's sign-in page. PayPal sends the seller back to `/api/account/paypal/callback`, which signs them in (creating the account the first time), records the PayPal account their sales are paid into, and redirects to `next`.
+ Parameters
    + next (string, optional)

        A path on this site to land on afterwards. Defaults to `/account`.

        + Sample: /account

+ Response 302 

        To PayPal's sign-in page.




+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Log in with PayPal isn't switched on for this server.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)





# Group Shops

Create a shop and manage it as its seller.

## Api Shops [/api/shops]

### createShop [POST]
Starts a draft shop from one of three sources. Gemini designs the page and guesses the
setup; check it with `getShop`, adjust with `updateShop`, then go live.

Sent with a session cookie from `signIn`, the shop belongs to that account, which also
becomes its seller email (and PayPal email, after Log in with PayPal) unless you give one.

- `source=photo`: a `photo` and/or a `description` of your own product.
- `source=link`: a `url`. If Channel3 recognises it as a store's product page, the shop
  becomes a recommendation (`product_type: referral`); otherwise the page is read and you
  sell the product yourself with PayPal.
- `source=channel3`: a `productId` from `searchProducts` (a recommendation).

Takes 15–40 seconds. Hero art, if available, is generated afterwards (`hero_status`).

**Platforms:** sent with a platform API key, the shop belongs to the key's account, so the
key can manage it from then on (no need to keep the admin token). It's made for one of the
platform's sellers, so it inherits nothing from the account: set `paypal_email` or call
`connectPayPal` for that seller.
+ Attributes
    + source (enum[string], required)

        What the shop starts from: a photo (with an optional description), a product link, or a Channel3 product to recommend.

        + Members
            + `photo` 
            + `link` 
            + `channel3` 

    + photo (string, optional)

        `source=photo`: the product photo, up to 8 MB.

    + description (string, optional)

        `source=photo`: a sentence or two about the product. Required if there is no photo.

        + Sample: Vintage cream and red quad roller skates with walnut burl heels.
    + url (string, optional)

        `source=link`: a product page, or your own app or game page.

        + Sample: https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates
    + productId (string, optional)

        `source=channel3`: a product id from `searchProducts`.

        + Sample: ch3_7f2a9c1e
    + slug (string, optional)

        The link name you want. If omitted, the AI suggests one.

        + Sample: vintageskates
    + type (enum[string], optional)

        `physical` ships, `digital` is a file or an access code, `auto` lets the AI decide.

        + Default: auto
        + Members
            + `auto` 
            + `physical` 
            + `digital` 

    + delivery (enum[string], optional)

        For digital products. If omitted, the AI guesses.

        + Members
            + `file` 
            + `access_code` 

    + access_url (string, optional)

        Where buyers use an access code.

        + Sample: https://www.miriogames.com/raptor-rush/
    + price (number, optional)

        USD. If omitted, the AI suggests a price.

        + Sample: 240
    + shipping (number, optional)

        Physical products: shipping per order, in USD. If omitted, the AI suggests it.

        + Sample: 15
    + stock (number, optional)

        How many are for sale. Leave out for unlimited.

        + Sample: 7
    + ship_countries (string, optional)

        Physical products: comma-separated ISO country codes to ship to. Empty means anywhere PayPal ships.

    + paypal_email (string, optional)

        The PayPal account that gets paid, if the seller doesn't connect one with `connectPayPal`.

        + Sample: seller@example.com
    + seller_email (string, optional)

        Where order notifications go.

        + Sample: seller@example.com
    + digital_file (string, optional)

        Digital products sold as a file: the file buyers download, up to 25 MB. Can also be added later with `uploadDigitalFile`.


+ Request (multipart/form-data)




+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Draft created.

    + Attributes (CreatedShop)


    + Body

            {"slug":"vintageskates","token":"3fJ9xQm2LwP8vR1tZk7cN4bY6dHs0aEu","manageUrl":"/manage/vintageskates?token=3fJ9xQm2LwP8vR1tZk7cN4bY6dHs0aEu"}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 409 (application/json)

        Taken or unavailable (a link name, or a sold-out product).

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Sold out."}


+ Response 429 (application/json)

        Over this network's cap for the call (see **Limits**). Retry after `Retry-After` seconds.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Too many checkouts from your network. Try again in 7 min."}


+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}



## Api Shops By Slug [/api/shops/{slug}]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: vintageskates

### getShop [GET]
Everything about the shop, including the AI's design spec and guesses.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The shop.

    + Attributes (Shop)


    + Body

            {"id":"Hn2c8QvL0xTzR4pW","slug":"vintageskates","status":"live","product_type":"physical","price_cents":24000,"currency":"USD","shipping_cents":1500,"ship_countries":"US","stock":null,"delivery":"file","access_url":null,"paypal_email":"seller@example.com","seller_email":"seller@example.com","paypal_merchant_id":"7MZJ4QXN8K2LA","paypal_status":{"receivable":true,"emailConfirmed":true,"checkedAt":"2026-10-21T18:04:11Z"},"zapier_hook_url":null,"in_gallery":true,"account_id":"Vq3nN8cT0bLx2YwE","options":[{"name":"Size","kind":"size","values":[{"label":"7"},{"label":"8"},{"label":"9"}]}],"option_stock":{"7":3,"8":0,"9":6},"suggestions":null,"photo_blob":"LFRvGuTU3D8i334X","gallery_blobs":["zrySajNyao6_j11x","SuqcgNv64HWN8H6e"],"hero_blob":null,"hero_status":"none","hero_error":null,"ai_source":"gemini","source_url":null,"referral":null,"spec":{"productType":"physical","productName":"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates","layout":"editorial","palette":{"background":"#f6efe4","surface":"#fffaf2","text":"#2b1d14","muted":"#7a6455","accent":"#b3261e","accentText":"#ffffff"},"fonts":{"heading":"Playfair Display","body":"Inter"},"eyebrow":"One pair, restored","headline":"Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels","subheadline":"A vintage pair of skates featuring cream leather, bold red trim, and durable quad wheels.","story":"Each pair combines soft cream leather with distinct red accents and a sculpted walnut burl heel base.","bullets":["Handmade cream leather upper with rich red trim","Sculpted walnut burl heel structure for stability"],"details":[{"label":"Materials","value":"Leather upper, walnut burl heel, rubber wheels"}],"faq":[{"q":"Are these suitable for outdoor skating?","a":"Yes, on indoor rink floors and paved outdoor paths."}],"ctaLabel":"Buy the skates","suggestedPriceUsd":240,"suggestedShippingUsd":15,"imageAlt":"Cream leather quad roller skates with red trim"},"created_at":"2026-10-19T15:22:08Z"}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


### updateShop [PATCH]
Changes only the fields you send. Renaming `slug` keeps the old link working (it
redirects). Set `status: live` to publish; a digital product needs its file (or, for
access codes, `access_url`) first.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (ShopUpdate)


    + Body

            {
                "status": "live"
            }


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Saved.

    + Attributes (Api Shops Response)


    + Body

            {"ok":true,"slug":"vintageskates"}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}



