## Api Orders [/api/orders]

### createCheckoutOrder [POST]
Creates the PayPal order for one unit of a live shop's product. The amount always comes
from the shop, never from the caller. Pass the returned `id` to the PayPal JS SDK.

If the shop has buyer `options`, send one value for each. A sold-out combination answers 409.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Orders Request)


    + Body

            {
                "slug": "raptorrush"
            }


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        PayPal order created.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Response)


    + Body

            {"id":"5O190127TN364715T"}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


+ Response 409 (application/json)

        Taken or unavailable (a link name, or a sold-out product).

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Sold out."}


+ Response 429 (application/json)

        Over this network's cap for the call (see **Limits**). Retry after `Retry-After` seconds.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Too many checkouts from your network. Try again in 7 min."}


+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}



## Api Orders Capture By PaypalOrderId [/api/orders/{paypalOrderId}/capture]

+ Parameters
    + paypalOrderId (string, required)

        The PayPal order id that `createCheckoutOrder` returned.

        + Sample: 5O190127TN364715T

### captureCheckoutOrder [POST]
Call after the buyer approves. Records the sale; digital orders get a download link or access code.
Safe to call repeatedly: before approval it answers 409, so a page can poll it while the PayPal window is open.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Paid.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Capture Response)


    + Body

            {"orderId":"pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe","status":"paid"}


+ Response 402 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


+ Response 409 (application/json)

        The buyer hasn't approved the order yet.

    + Attributes (Api Orders Capture 409 Error1)



+ Response 410 (application/json)

        The last unit (or the last of the buyer's combination) sold while they were paying, or the PayPal checkout expired before they paid. The payment isn't captured, so the buyer isn't charged.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)



+ Response 422 (application/json)

        The buyer's funding source was declined (`INSTRUMENT_DECLINED`); they can try another.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)



+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (ErrorResponse)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}




