**Raptor Rush: Browser Edition**: $2.99. Grow from Tiny Hatchling to Giant Apex Predator
Which one?` (string, optional) - A suggested reply to the buyer, in Markdown with the links already written as links: the product and its options to pick from, the pay link, or what they got with a receipt link. Buyers have the best experience when agents show it as written.
+ `agent_name`: `Grok` (string, optional) - Who this request was credited to in the seller's stats: a recognised user agent, else the name the agent gave itself (`?agent=`, or the MCP client's name), else the user agent's first word.
+ `order_id`: `pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe` (string, required) - The order's id.
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - `declined`: PayPal declined it, nothing charged, the buyer can open `pay_url` again. `sold_out`: it sold out before the payment was captured. `expired`: the PayPal checkout expired; create a new order. `failed`: PayPal couldn't be reached; ask again.
    + `awaiting_buyer_approval`
    + `paid`
    + `declined`
    + `sold_out`
    + `expired`
    + `failed`
+ `product`: `Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates` (string, required) - The product's name.
+ `options`: `{"Size":"M","Color":"Black"}` (string, optional) - The buyer's pick, one value per option, keyed by option name.
+ `amount` (Amount, required) - What the order costs, as numbers.
+ `total`: `$255.00` (string, required) - The total as a label, e.g. `$255.00`.
+ `pay_url`: `https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/o/pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe` (string, optional) - Unpaid orders (waiting or declined). The buyer pays here; safe to show in chat.
+ `next_step`: `Show pay_url to the buyer as a link. When they say they've paid, call get_order with order_id.` (string, optional) - Unpaid orders. What the agent should do next, in plain words.
+ `paid_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, optional) - Paid orders. When PayPal captured the payment.
+ `receipt_url`: `https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates/thanks?order=pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe` (string, optional) - Paid orders. The buyer's thank-you page.
+ `delivery`: `{"type":"access_code","access_code":"K7QF-M2XP-9HTD","start_url":"https://www.miriogames.com/raptor-rush/?code=K7QF-M2XP-9HTD"}` (string, optional) - Paid orders. What the buyer got.


## AgentDeliveryAccessCode (object)
A digital product unlocked with an access code.

### Properties
+ `type`: `access_code` (string, required) - Always `access_code`.
+ `access_code`: `K7QF-M2XP-9HTD` (string, required) - The buyer's code, which unlocks the seller's app or game.
+ `start_url`: `https://www.miriogames.com/raptor-rush/?code=K7QF-M2XP-9HTD` (string, optional) - The seller's app with the code filled in.


## AgentDeliveryDownload (object)
A digital file to download.

### Properties
+ `type`: `download` (string, required) - Always `download`.
+ `download_url`: `https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/download/dl_4mQ8sT2vX9` (string, required) - A private link to the file. It works 5 times over 14 days.
+ `note`: `Works 5 times over 14 days.` (string, optional) - How long the link lasts and how many downloads it allows, in words.


## AgentDeliveryShipping (object)
A physical product shipped to the buyer.

### Properties
+ `type`: `shipping` (string, required) - Always `shipping`.
+ `ship_to` (ShipTo, optional, nullable) - Where it ships, from the buyer's PayPal checkout. Null if PayPal didn't share it.
+ `fulfillment` (enum[string], required) - `to_ship` until the seller adds tracking, then `shipped`.
    + `to_ship`
    + `shipped`
+ `tracking` (Tracking, optional, nullable) - The carrier and tracking number once shipped; null before.


## PlatformShop (object)
A shop as a platform API key lists it.

### Properties
+ `slug`: `vintageskates` (string, required) - The shop's link name.
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - `draft` until the seller goes live.
    + `draft`
    + `live`
+ `name`: `Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates` (string, required) - The product's name.
+ `headline`: `Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels` (string, optional) - The shop's one-line pitch.
+ `product_type` (enum[string], required) - `physical`, `digital` or `referral`.
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `price` (AgentMoney, required) - An amount of money, as a number and as a label.
+ `url`: `https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates` (string, required) - The shop page buyers pay on.
+ `cover`: `https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X` (string, optional, nullable) - The cover image's URL.
+ `paypal_connected`: `true` (boolean, required) - The seller connected a PayPal account that can be paid.
+ `sales`: `12` (number, required) - Paid orders.
+ `created_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, required) - When the shop was made.


## AgentMoney (object)
An amount of money, as a number and as a label.

### Properties
+ `amount`: `48.5` (number, required) - The amount in the currency's main unit (dollars, not cents).
+ `currency`: `USD` (string, required) - ISO 4217 currency code.
+ `label`: `$48.50` (string, optional) - The amount formatted for people.


## JsonRpcRequest (object)
A JSON-RPC 2.0 request to the MCP server.

### Properties
+ `jsonrpc`: `2.0` (string, required) - Always `2.0`.
+ `id`: `1` (string, optional, nullable) - Leave out for a notification.
+ `method` (enum[string], required) - The MCP method. `tools/call` runs a tool; `tools/list` lists them.
    + `initialize`
    + `ping`
    + `tools/list`
    + `tools/call`
    + `notifications/initialized`
+ `params`: `{"name":"get_product","arguments":{"shop":"vintageskates"}}` (object, optional) - For `tools/call`: `{ name, arguments }`.


## JsonRpcResponse (object)
A JSON-RPC 2.0 reply from the MCP server.

### Properties
+ `jsonrpc`: `2.0` (string, required) - Always `2.0`.
+ `id`: `1` (string, required, nullable) - The request's `id`.
+ `result`: `{"isError":false}` (object, optional) - For `tools/call`: `content` (the answer as JSON text), `structuredContent` (the same object) and `isError`.
+ `error` (Error, optional) - Present when the call failed.


## Referral (object)
A recommended Channel3 product. Buy links are Channel3-tracked, credited to this shop.

### Properties
+ `productId`: `ch3_7f2a9c1e` (string, required) - Channel3's product id.
+ `title`: `Trail Running Vest 5L` (string, required) - The product's name.
+ `brand`: `Salomon` (string, optional, nullable) - The brand, when known.
+ `image`: `https://images.example.com/vest.jpg` (string, optional, nullable) - The product image's URL.
+ `offers` (array[Offer], required) - Stores that sell it, with tracked links.


## ProductCard (object)
A Channel3 product in search results.

### Properties
+ `id`: `ch3_7f2a9c1e` (string, required) - Channel3's product id: pass it to `createShop` as `productId`.
+ `title`: `Trail Running Vest 5L` (string, required) - The product's name.
+ `brand`: `Salomon` (string, optional, nullable) - The brand, when known.
+ `image`: `https://images.example.com/vest.jpg` (string, required) - The product image's URL.
+ `price`: `240` (number, required) - The best offer's price.
+ `currency`: `USD` (string, required) - ISO 4217 currency code.
+ `retailer`: `rei.com` (string, required) - The store with the best offer.
+ `retailers`: `4` (number, required) - How many stores sell it.
+ `commission`: `0.08` (number, required) - Best commission rate across offers, 0–1.


## Order (object)
An order, as the seller sees it.

### Properties
+ `id`: `pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe` (string, required) - OneThing's order id.
+ `paypal_order_id`: `5O190127TN364715T` (string, optional, nullable) - PayPal's order id.
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - `created` until paid; `failed` if PayPal declined; `refunded` after a refund.
    + `created`
    + `paid`
    + `failed`
    + `refunded`
+ `amount_cents`: `25500` (number, required) - The total charged, shipping included, in cents.
+ `shipping_cents`: `1500` (number, optional) - The shipping part of `amount_cents`.
+ `currency`: `USD` (string, required) - ISO 4217 currency code.
+ `buyer_email`: `sam@example.com` (string, optional, nullable) - From PayPal, once paid.
+ `buyer_name`: `Sam Rivera` (string, optional, nullable) - From PayPal, once paid.
+ `shipping_address`: `{"address_line_1":"1 Main St","admin_area_2":"Springfield","admin_area_1":"IL","postal_code":"62701","country_code":"US"}` (string, optional, nullable) - Physical orders: the address from PayPal checkout, by field.
+ `capture_id`: `3C679366HH908993F` (string, optional, nullable) - PayPal's capture id, once paid. Refunds use it.
+ `fulfillment_status` (enum[string], required) - `to_ship` and `shipped` for physical orders, `digital_sent` for digital ones, `none` before payment.
    + `none`
    + `to_ship`
    + `shipped`
    + `digital_sent`
+ `carrier`: `USPS` (string, optional, nullable) - Shipped orders: the carrier.
+ `tracking_number`: `9400111899223197428490` (string, optional, nullable) - Shipped orders: the tracking number.
+ `tracking_synced`: `false` (boolean, optional) - Whether PayPal accepted the tracking number.
+ `downloads`: `0` (number, optional) - How many times the buyer downloaded the file.
+ `access_code`: `K7QF-M2XP-9HTD` (string, optional, nullable) - Access-code products: the code this buyer got.
+ `code_uses`: `0` (number, optional) - How many times the access code was checked.
+ `code_last_used_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, optional, nullable) - When the access code was last checked with `verifyAccessCode`.
+ `channel` (enum[string], optional) - `agent` for orders an AI agent placed (MCP or an order link).
    + `web`
    + `agent`
+ `agent`: `Grok` (string, optional, nullable) - The agent credited with an agent order, such as `Grok`.
+ `refund_id`: `1JU08902781691411` (string, optional, nullable) - PayPal's refund id, once refunded through OneThing.
+ `refunded_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, optional, nullable) - When the order was refunded.
+ `options`: `{"Size":"9"}` (string, optional, nullable) - The buyer's pick, one value per option, keyed by option name (see `Choice`).
+ `paid_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, optional, nullable) - When PayPal captured the payment.
+ `created_at`: `2026-10-22T02:41:37Z` (string, optional) - When the order was made.


